{
  "_comment": [
    "Class, spec and stat-weight definitions. This is the file to edit when a ranking looks wrong",
    "for reasons of valuation; edit config/overrides.json instead when a single item is wrong for",
    "reasons the maths cannot see (set bonuses, procs, weapon-speed breakpoints).",
    "",
    "Weights are expressed in attack-power-equivalent units for physical specs and in spell-power-",
    "equivalent units for casters and healers, i.e. the primary throughput stat always has weight",
    "1.0 and everything else is relative to it. Absolute scale does not matter, only ratios.",
    "",
    "'school' makes school-specific gear score correctly: the engine computes effective spell power",
    "as spellPower + spellDmg<school>, so '+30 Fire Damage' counts fully for a Fire mage and not at",
    "all for a Frost one, without double-counting generic '+30 Spell Damage'.",
    "",
    "A cap entry means value above 'cap' is scored at 'postCapWeight' instead of the full weight.",
    "This is applied per item, which is an approximation - see README."
  ],

  "statKeys": [
    "str", "agi", "sta", "int", "spi", "armor",
    "ap", "rap", "spellPower", "healPower",
    "hit", "crit", "spellHit", "spellCrit", "spellPen", "mp5", "mp5WhileCasting",
    "haste", "armorPen",
    "defense", "dodge", "parry", "block", "blockValue",
    "resFire", "resNature", "resFrost", "resShadow", "resArcane",
    "weaponDps", "rangedDps"
  ],

  "_extraStatsComment": [
    "haste is percent attack speed, armorPen is flat armour ignored, and mp5WhileCasting is the",
    "percentage of mana regeneration that continues while casting. All three come from Equip lines",
    "rather than the base stat block. Weight them per spec; a spec that omits a key simply scores",
    "it as zero."
  ],

  "_defaultsComment": [
    "Baseline weights merged underneath every spec's own, so the handful of stats that behave the",
    "same across a whole archetype are stated once. A spec's own weights always win.",
    "Archetype is derived: role 'healer' -> healer, role 'tank' -> tank, a dps spec with a 'school'",
    "-> caster, anything else -> melee."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "melee":  { "haste": 14, "armorPen": 0.15, "leech": 2 },
    "caster": { "mp5WhileCasting": 0.8 },
    "healer": { "mp5WhileCasting": 1.5 },
    "tank":   { "haste": 4, "armorPen": 0, "leech": 4 }
  },

